---
/**
 * TEACHING & LEARNING · SMART CLASSROOMS & DIGITAL LITERACY — audit §2C.
 *
 * ⚠ COMBINED PAGE — two of the brief's fourteen bullets: Smart Classrooms and
 * AI & Digital Literacy. The standalone /ai-digital-literacy/ route was an
 * implementation experiment; its verified content is merged here and the route
 * is retired.
 *
 * ⚠⚠ AN ERROR FROM THE SPLIT PAGE IS NOT CARRIED OVER. That page read: "75+
 * digitally smart classrooms and 49+ interactive flat panels — MORE PANELS THAN
 * ROOMS." Forty-nine is fewer than seventy-five. The true and more interesting
 * statement is the opposite one, and it is made honestly below: the panels do
 * not yet reach every smart classroom. A school that publishes both numbers has
 * given a reader the means to notice, and writing past it would have been the
 * one thing worse than not mentioning it.
 *
 * ═══ SOURCE — verified in this repository ══════════════════════════════════
 *   75+ digitally smart classrooms · 49+ interactive flat panels
 *     (data/academics.ts counters, and `facilities` — "75+ rooms · 49+
 *     interactive flat panels").
 *   100 Microsoft Innovative Educator Experts → a Microsoft Showcase School.
 *   Junior and senior computer laboratories, 40+ machines each.
 *   Indian AI Impact Festival, 2024 — Ayushi, of Class VII, placed first.
 *   The Reading Carnival photograph shows the school's own wall of "Microsoft
 *     Innovative Educator Expert 2024" posters — the certification is displayed
 *     in the building, not only stated on a website.
 *
 * ⚠ NOT CLAIMED: a device-per-child ratio, a rollout date for the remaining
 * rooms, an AI syllabus, or which classes take digital literacy. None is
 * published.
 *
 * ⚠ SCOPE BOUNDARY — the METHOD that runs on this equipment is Teaching
 * Methodology's; the Robotics Lab and the national science programmes are STEM,
 * Robotics & Enrichment's. This page is the room and the subject.
 *
 * Composition: split (ivory, photo RIGHT) → collage (paper, LEFT — the numbers)
 * → statement (sand — the honest gap) → close.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../../components/ui/PageHero.astro';
import AcSplit from '../../../components/academics/system/AcSplit.astro';
import AcCollage from '../../../components/academics/system/AcCollage.astro';
import AcStatement from '../../../components/academics/system/AcStatement.astro';
import AcClose from '../../../components/academics/system/AcClose.astro';

import banner from '../../../assets/computer lab/DSC_1204 copy.jpg';
import pComputers from '../../../assets/computer lab/DSC_1204 copy.jpg';
import pComp2 from '../../../assets/computer lab/DSC_1206 copy.jpg';
import pCanva from '../../../assets/school-event/Impetus—ClassesIII-V/Impetus—ClassesIII-V-02.jpg';
import pCarnival from '../../../assets/school-event/Reading-Carnival/Reading-Carnival-02.jpg';
import pCohort from '../../../assets/photos/sunbeem-3.jpg';

const school = 'Sunbeam School Ballia';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Smart Classrooms & Digital Literacy — Sunbeam School Ballia"
  description="Digital teaching at Sunbeam School Ballia: 75+ smart classrooms, 49+ interactive flat panels, two computer laboratories with 40+ machines each, and 100 Microsoft Innovative Educator Experts."
>
  <PageHero
    title="Smart Classrooms & Digital Literacy"
    standfirst="The certification is the teachers, not the hardware — a hundred of them."
    crumbs={[
      { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
      { label: 'Academics', href: '/academics/' },
      { label: 'Teaching & Learning', href: '/academics/teaching-learning/' },
    ]}
    src={banner}
    alt="The computer laboratory at Sunbeam School Ballia, its machines set out along the benches."
    position="50% 50%"
  />

  <div class="u-page-panel ac-panel">
    <AcSplit
      ground="ivory"
      side="right"
      aspect="3 / 2"
      kicker="The room"
      heading="Standard equipment,<br /><em>not a showcase room</em>"
      body={[
        'The useful question about a smart classroom is not whether the school has one. It is whether a teacher can assume it. Sunbeam publishes <strong>75+ digitally smart classrooms</strong> — a number at the scale of the whole school rather than of a demonstration suite booked by rotation.',
        'Alongside them the school runs <strong>two computer laboratories</strong>, junior and senior, carrying <strong>40+ machines each</strong>. The junior room is where nine-year-olds are taught presentation software under the Impetus programme — the session photographed here is one of its sittings.',
      ]}
      photo={pComputers}
      alt={`The computer laboratory at ${school}, its machines set out along the benches`}
      inset={pCanva}
      insetAlt={`A class at ${school} during a Canva Presentation activity in the Impetus programme, the interactive board in use behind them`}
    />

    <AcCollage
      ground="paper"
      side="left"
      kicker="And the part that is not equipment"
      heading="A hundred teachers,<br /><em>certified by Microsoft</em>"
      body={[
        'A panel does nothing on its own. What makes Sunbeam Ballia a <strong>Microsoft Showcase School</strong> is that <strong>one hundred of its teachers</strong> hold Microsoft Innovative Educator Expert certification — a credential issued by somebody other than the school.',
        'It is not a website claim either. The school displays the MIE Expert posters along a corridor wall, which is where the photograph on the right was taken — the certification is up in the building where parents walk past it.',
        'Digital literacy then arrives as <strong>a subject with its own time</strong> rather than as a word attached to existing lessons, and it produces results: <strong>Ayushi, of Class VII, placed first at the Indian AI Impact Festival in 2024</strong>.',
      ]}
      ledger={[
        { k: 'Smart classrooms', v: '75+ digitally smart classrooms across the school.' },
        { k: 'Interactive flat panels', v: '49+ panels — see the note below on what that number means.' },
        { k: 'Computer laboratories', v: 'Two, junior and senior, 40+ machines each.' },
        { k: 'Microsoft Showcase School', v: '100 teachers certified as Microsoft Innovative Educator Experts.' },
        { k: 'Indian AI Impact Festival · 2024', v: 'Ayushi, of Class VII, placed <strong>first</strong>.' },
      ]}
      lead={{ src: pCarnival, alt: `A corridor at ${school} during the Reading Carnival, the school’s Microsoft Innovative Educator Expert 2024 posters displayed on the wall behind the book racks` }}
      support={[
        { src: pComp2, alt: `The computer laboratory at ${school}, its machines set out along the benches` },
        { src: pCanva, alt: `A class at ${school} during a Canva Presentation activity, the interactive board in use` },
      ]}
    />

    <AcStatement
      ground="sand"
      ghost="49 / 75"
      ghostAt="left"
      texture={true}
      kicker="What the two numbers mean together"
      statement="Not every room,<br /><em>yet.</em>"
      body={[
        'The school publishes both figures, so both are printed here: <strong>75+ smart classrooms</strong> and <strong>49+ interactive flat panels</strong>. Read together they say something the marketing sentence would not — <em>the panels do not yet reach every room.</em>',
        'That is worth stating plainly rather than writing around. A parent comparing schools is entitled to know that this is a rollout in progress rather than a finished one, and a school that publishes both numbers has already given them the means to work it out.',
        'It is also the more credible claim. Forty-nine panels in seventy-five rooms is a real school spending real money over several years; a page asserting one in every room, with nothing to check it against, would be worth less.',
      ]}
    />

    <AcClose
      owed={true}
      statement="A hundred teachers,<br /><em>certified elsewhere.</em>"
      body="The school publishes its room counts, its panel count and the certification behind them. It does not publish a device-per-child ratio, a rollout schedule for the remaining rooms, or which classes take digital literacy and for how long."
      photo={pCohort}
      alt={`Students and staff of ${school} gathered on the hall stage`}
      position="50% 42%"
    />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  div.ac-panel { padding-block: 0; }
</style>
